From cc012f63d089bd28cd59a5dc5ec795bf9b90e46a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:22:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 36/51] objects: clamp negative TSC intervals, count them
 (build 72; verifier LOW)

Every TSC interval of the build-71 instrumentation (object sections, write
start/end, switch_rw, reclaim, read_seqlock_begin spin, NR waits) goes
through coh::Sub / waitstat::add: a negative delta (TSC skew across CPUs or
between nested timestamps) is clamped to 0 and counted per thread;
ObjectThreadCoh.reserved[2] = C++ + NR count. Observation only, no protocol
change. object-test logs the count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
